   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to dedicating a portion of the\nstate highway system to East Fishkill veterans",
    "basePrintNo": "S9505",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9505-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §345-e, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9505\n\nSPONSOR: ROLISON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to dedicating a portion of\nthe state highway system to East Fishkill veterans\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nDedicates a portion of the state highway system to East Fishkill veter-\nans.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. - Adds a new section 345-e to the highway law dedicating a\nportion of state route 376 in the town of East Fishkill, from state\nroute 82 to state route 52, to East Fishkill veterans.\n\nSection 2. - Directs the commissioner of transportation to install and\nmaintain adequate signing stating \"Highway Dedicated to East Fishkill\nVeterans\". Clarifies that the dedication is ceremonial and the official\nname of the highway shall not be changed.\n\nSection 3. - Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill seeks to honor the brave individuals from East Fishkill who\nhave served in the United States Armed Forces. By dedicating this\nspecific portion of State Route 376 to East Fishkill veterans, the state\nprovides a lasting, visible tribute to their sacrifices and dedication\nto our country. Ceremonial highway dedications serve as a daily reminder\nto the community of the local heroes who have protected our freedoms.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
